Lambda Enterprises: publishing to paulnapierskie.com

This folder holds three files:

index.html: the whole website
CNAME: tells GitHub Pages to serve it at paulnapierskie.com
README.md: these steps
Before you publish

Search index.html for square brackets and replace each placeholder:

[YOUR EMAIL ADDRESS] (appears 3 times)
[CITY, STATE] (appears 2 times)
[PROJECT TITLE], [SERVICE] and the one-sentence description (3 project cards)
[ARTICLE TITLE], [TOPIC], [YEAR] (3 insight rows)
[PROJECT IMAGE] boxes (replace with <img> tags, or leave as blank panels)
Publish with GitHub Pages
Create a free account at github.com and make a new public repository, for example lambda-site.
Upload all three files (Add file, then Upload files). Keep CNAME exactly as named, with no extension.
Open the repository's Settings, then Pages. Under Source choose Deploy from a branch, pick main and / (root), and save.
Under Custom domain, enter paulnapierskie.com and save. Tick Enforce HTTPS once it becomes available.
Point your domain at GitHub

In your registrar's DNS settings, add these records:

Type	Host	Value
A	@	185.199.108.153
A	@	185.199.109.153
A	@	185.199.110.153
A	@	185.199.111.153
CNAME	www	YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME.github.io
